is my name is aziza  i'm 32 and the hazara from ghazni  province  in kabul i worked as a tailor for an  american company  and then at the afghan defense ministry  but i had to leave  afghanistan i received  threatening calls and we were followed  even in the car  it was dangerous one of our staff passes  was blown up by a suicide bomber  my work was in the shash dark area of  kabul where the afghan intel office and  the us embassy were also located  i was traumatized when i saw the bodies  of the journalists killed in the attack  there aren't jobs or a good working  environment for most women in  afghanistan  i worked six years for the government  but it was hard for me to continue  in my work environment it was mostly men  people would talk about us the taliban  would also follow our staff  car or bus from the ministry so i left  recently about 25 girls were taken by  the taliban from the malistan district  of kazna province  and they were forced into marriage  i arrived in iran on a visa and then we  were smuggled into turkey  the journey was very dangerous and  difficult i was thinking at one point i  might die  but god helped me from iran to turkey we  paid  one thousand dollars each  i want peace and prosperity for my  country we're tired of wars  but that's all i've seen since i was a  child and i don't expect peace in  afghanistan anytime soon  i want to move to a safer place where we  can live in peace  it will be better for us
 

